claims:
1. A method for producing a ranking for pages on the web, comprising:
receiving a plurality of web pages, wherein the plurality of web pages are inter-linked with page links;
receiving n seed pages, each seed page including at least one outgoing link to a respective web page in the plurality of web pages, wherein n is an integer greater than one;
assigning, by one or more computers, a respective length to each page link and each outgoing link;
identifying, by the one or more computers and from among the n seed pages, a kth-closest seed page to a first web page in the plurality of web pages according to the lengths of the links, wherein k is greater than one and less than n;
determining a ranking score for the first web page from a shortest distance from the kth-closest seed page to the first web page; and
producing a ranking for the first web page from the ranking score.

12. A non-transitory computer-readable storage medium storing instructions that when executed by a computer cause the computer to perform operations comprising:
receiving a plurality of web pages, wherein the plurality of web pages are inter-linked with page links;
receiving n seed pages, each seed page including at least one outgoing link to a respective web page in the plurality of web pages, wherein n is an integer greater than one;
assigning a respective length to each page link and each outgoing link;
identifying, from among the n seed pages, a kth-closest seed page to a first web page in the plurality of web pages according to the lengths of the links, wherein k is greater than one less than n;
determining a ranking score for the first web page from a shortest distance from the kth-closest seed page to the first web page; and
producing a ranking for the first web page from the ranking score.

23. A system, comprising:
one or more computers coupled to one or more storage devices storing instructions that when executed by the one or more computers cause the one or more computers to perform operations comprising:
receiving a plurality of web pages to be ranked, wherein the plurality of web pages are inter-linked with page links;
receiving n seed pages, each seed page including at least one outgoing link to a respective web page in the plurality of web pages, wherein n is an integer greater than one;
assigning a respective length to each page link;
identifying, from among the n seed pages, a kth-closest seed page to a first web page in the plurality of web pages according to the lengths of the links, wherein k is an integer greater than one and less than n;
determining a ranking score for the first web page from a shortest distance from the kth-closest seed page to the first web page; and
producing a ranking for the first web page from the ranking score.
